## Claim under pressure
SPRINT **7.2** (CRIT): `c_sys_exec_last_arg` extracts the last top-level C
arg span for `sys_exec` sink refuse (argv beyond a0/a1/a2). Zero-trust
gates for **this** close (not 7.1 ident walker, not T1 return taint):

| # | Gate | Expectation |
|---|------|-------------|
| Z1 | SECRET last argv fail-closed | Bare SECRET IDENT as last `sys_exec` argv → `ERR\tsecret` + rc≠0 |
| Z2 | Quote-split cannot hide unquoted SECRET IDENT | Commas / `\\` / `\"` inside `"..."` must not move `last_start` past a following bare SECRET, nor leave that IDENT `in_str` |
| Z3 | No fail-open if last-arg helper returns empty | Empty extract must not skip refuse when a last SECRET IDENT is present |
| Z4 | Do not reopen 7.1 | Ident-scan walker stays closed; this audit does not retarget it |

Adversarial stance: treat last-arg string/escape/depth skip as a **desync
weapon** until proved that an unquoted SECRET after a well-formed C string
still refuses. Treat `if last != ""` as a **fail-open skip** until the
helper is shown never to return `""` **and** a backup rail still refuses.

